    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9903" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-corpŏro</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to unite in one body, to incorporate</i>
			(except in Pliny the elder, only in late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid cum melle,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					22, 24, 53, § 113</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitiligines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					27, 12, 90, § 112</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scopuli concorporati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 22, 8, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">concorporatus ecclesiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Pud. 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">medicamen concorporatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Marc. Emp. 36</span></i>
			.</div>
